      "itemDescription": "<span style=\"font-weight: 400\">The Teachers Insurance and Annuity Association of America (TIAA) is a major provider of insurance and retirement-savings accounts, especially to people working in academia, education, and state and local government. Founded by Andrew Carnegie in 1918, the company has about 5 million customers nationwide and $1.4 trillion in assets under management. Revenue sagged by 2.6% at TIAA in 2021, but profits grew robustly, and the company announced plans to add as many as 2,000 new jobs at a new corporate center in Frisco, Texas.</span>",
      "uri": "/ranking/fortune500/2022/",
      "__typename": "_ItemRankingListsType"
    },
